   "evidence": "CubeBoundary.lean: `-- Transparency lets importers use OrthonormalBasis.equiv_apply_basis directly. @[expose] def equatorIsometry`. Generator.lean `equator_basis_naturality` passes `fun i \u21a6 OrthonormalBasis.equiv_apply_basis (stdBasis (n+1)) (stdBasis (n+2)).orthogonalLast (Equiv.refl _) i` as `hf : \u2200 i, f (b i) = c i` (Sphere.lean:540). That only typechecks if `equatorIsometry` unfolds.",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicTopology/Disk/CubeBoundary.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public `@[simp] equatorIsometry_apply_basis` stating `equatorIsometry n (((EuclideanSpace.basisFun _ \u211d).reindex Equiv.ulift) i) = (((EuclideanSpace.basisFun _ \u211d).reindex Equiv.ulift).orthogonalLast) i`, proved by `OrthonormalBasis.equiv_apply_basis`. Then remove `@[expose]` and change `equator_basis_naturality` to use the new lemma.",
   "issue": "`equatorIsometry` is `@[expose]`, and the comment says this is so importers can apply `OrthonormalBasis.equiv_apply_basis` by unfolding it. That exposes the body because a lemma is missing. Its one consumer, `equator_basis_naturality` in Cube/Generator.lean, needs exactly `\u2200 i, equatorIsometry n (stdBasis i) = (stdBasis (n+1)).orthogonalLast i`, which is the `hf` hypothesis of `reducedSingularHomologySphereIso_hom_naturality`.",
   "line": 228
  }
